WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.440
Stunt performers are the unsung heroes&nbsp;
of Hollywood productions — and Ahsoka's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.280
are some of the finest in the biz. So&nbsp;
who are the faces behind the fights?

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.480
Standing in as the stunt double&nbsp;
for a lead protagonist is no easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.880
job — especially when that protagonist is&nbsp;
also a former Jedi. Rosario Dawson handles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.660
the majority of Ahsoka's scenes in the&nbsp;
series, including a lot of the action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.560
but she doesn't do it all. That's&nbsp;
where Michelle C. Lee comes in.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.480
Though Lee is an immensely skilled martial&nbsp;
artist and stuntwoman, she's also a talented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.640
actor in her own right. You may know her from&nbsp;
her role as Oksana in 2021's Black Widow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.440
or as Violet on the Paramount+ adventure&nbsp;
series Blood &amp; Treasure. Lee's stunt credits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.080
are extensive, including everything from Top&nbsp;
Gun: Maverick to Suicide Squad to Pacific Rim.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.160
Beyond film and television, Lee has&nbsp;
also contributed her skills as a motion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.720
capture artist to a number of major video&nbsp;
games. Those credits include Uncharted:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.500
The Lost Legacy, The Last of Us:&nbsp;
Left Behind, and most notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.640
the Mortal Kombat series. Lee has worked&nbsp;
extensively in the latter franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.700
even playing Mileena in the 2013 web series Mortal&nbsp;
Kombat: Legacy. Perhaps it's no surprise, then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.860
that she was chosen to take on such an important&nbsp;
and intensive role during production on Ahsoka.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.660
Sabine Wren has a unique fighting style,&nbsp;
to say the least. She has trained under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:23.880
Jedi such as Kanan Jarrus and Ahsoka Tano,&nbsp;
as well as Mandalorians and even instructors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.440
at the Imperial Academy. As a result, her&nbsp;
approach in combat is something of a mishmash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.880
equal parts rebel bounty hunter,&nbsp;
Mandalorian warrior, and Jedi Knight.

00:01:33.236 --> 00:01:34.571
"Take us out… Padawan."

00:01:34.571 --> 00:01:39.420
While Natasha Liu Bordizzo does a lot of the work&nbsp;
in bringing that unique fighting style to life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:46.080
she has some help, too. Ahsoka Episode 7 credits&nbsp;
Chau Naumova as her stunt double — a younger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.620
performer who still seems to be making a&nbsp;
name for herself in Hollywood. Though she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:54.840
isn't marked as a stunt performer for the show&nbsp;
on IMDb, Naumova's page does also credits her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.800
as playing the role of Lieutenant Jensu,&nbsp;
one of the X-wing pilots who accompanies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.440
General Hera Syndulla to Seatos. That particular&nbsp;
squadron is apparently full of stunt performers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:09.360
as longtime Din Djarin stand-in Brendan&nbsp;
Wayne also flies a fighter in the same scene.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.460
Apart from Ahsoka, Naumova's only credit&nbsp;
on IMDb is for playing the Street Fighter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.900
character Ibuki in a low-budget&nbsp;
TV series. According to iStunt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:24.240
Naumova was also a competitor on Season&nbsp;
4 of NBC's World of Dance. Hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.980
her multiple roles in Ahsoka will help to elevate&nbsp;
her profile and career in the years to come.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.620
For a villain with the poise and presence of Ray&nbsp;
Stevenson's Baylan Skoll, you need a stunt double&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.840
equal to the task. And that's exactly what the&nbsp;
Ahsoka crew found when they hired Morgan Benoit.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.080
You may not know Benoit's name,&nbsp;
but you've almost surely seen his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.580
work. He was a stunt double for&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves in 2013's 47 Ronin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:53.280
and he has stunt credits on major action films&nbsp;
like Terminator: Dark Fate, Renfield, and Dune.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.760
All of those credits should have been&nbsp;
enough to get Benoit the role of Stevenson's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.600
stunt double on Ahsoka, but it probably&nbsp;
didn't hurt that he also had experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.040
in the Star Wars universe. He has performed&nbsp;
stunt work on The Mandalorian since 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.060
and he even lent his talents to the&nbsp;
big-budget video game Star Wars Jedi:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:14.400
Survivor earlier in 2023. In short, he was&nbsp;
the perfect man for the job — and Baylan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.660
Skoll's intense, aggressive lightsaber&nbsp;
fights stand as testament to that fact.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.340
Having worked on The Mandalorian probably&nbsp;
wasn't a requirement for stunt performers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.440
to get hired on Ahsoka, but it clearly wasn't&nbsp;
a mark against them. Morgan Benoit wasn't the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:32.460
only performer to move from one Star Wars&nbsp;
show to the other; Alicia Vela-Bailey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.820
the stunt double for Ivanna Sakhno's&nbsp;
character Shin Hati, did as well.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.600
In addition to her previous Star&nbsp;
Wars work, Vela-Bailey has earned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.380
credits as Gal Gadot's stunt double&nbsp;
for Wonder Woman and Batman v Superman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:48.420
Dawn of Justice. She also played a Themysciran&nbsp;
warrior early on in the first Wonder Woman movie.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.820
Star Wars isn't the only Disney franchise that&nbsp;
Vela-Bailey has experience in, either. She's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.680
true veteran of the Marvel universe, appearing&nbsp;
in several of the Netflix shows, including The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:04.140
Punisher and The Defenders, as well as Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 and Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:08.340
in which she also played the role of Alisha&nbsp;
Whitley. Vela-Bailey has lent her talents to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:13.380
Avatar franchise as well, playing a member of the&nbsp;
villainous Recom unit in Avatar: The Way of Water;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:19.020
on that production, she also worked as a stunt&nbsp;
double for both Sigourney Weaver and Zoe Saldana.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.500
Fans of Star Wars Rebels were more than elated at&nbsp;
the end of Ahsoka Episode 6, when Eman Esfandi's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:30.900
Ezra Bridger finally made his on screen debut. The&nbsp;
character is instantly recognizable as the beloved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:36.300
Jedi rogue from the animated series, and Esfandi&nbsp;
captures Ezra's spirit and personality perfectly.

00:04:36.585 --> 00:04:39.645
"The Force is my ally. It's all I need."

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:43.920
It was even more exciting for fans to see Ezra&nbsp;
leap into action in Ahsoka's seventh episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.820
on which Esfandi was assisted&nbsp;
by his stunt double, Jason Chu.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:53.340
Once again, we've got a Mandalorian alumnus here.&nbsp;
Chu has also worked on Disney projects such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.840
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. and Captain America:&nbsp;
Civil War, as well as multiple entries in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.340
modern Planet of the Apes franchise. He's been&nbsp;
particularly busy over the past several years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.140
lending his skills to movies such as&nbsp;
Army of the Dead, Blade Runner 2049,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:12.180
and Free Guy, among other projects. One&nbsp;
thing's for sure: He's not inexperienced.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:17.400
Ezra's Force-centric fighting style in Ahsoka is&nbsp;
a lot of fun to watch, and, if their social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:23.100
activity is any indication, Chu and Esfandi forged&nbsp;
a strong bond during production. The actor was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:28.800
commenting on his stunt double's Instagram posts&nbsp;
as recently as December 2022, pumping him up over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.480
some snazzy pics. But you'd expect nothing less&nbsp;
from the Ezra we all know and love, wouldn't you?

